          "abstract": "<jats:title>ABSTRACT</jats:title><jats:p>The paper reports on a large scale evaluation of two alternative models of undergraduate statistics courses. The traditional course orientation was compared with a problem\u2010solving orientation in which the emphasis was on real world problem\u2010solving, during the winter and spring quarters of 1973\u201374. The evaluation battery included behavioral and problem\u2010solving skill measures. The findings indicate that improvements in statistics programs can be made.</jats:p>",
          "DOI": "10.1111/j.1540-5915.1977.tb01083.x",
